---
// About (DESIGN_BRIEF.md 5.4).
//
// REORDERED 2026-10-08 (COPY-PASS-V1, Task 6), Kristen's copy pass:
//   a. Amy's headshot + the new About copy (headshot left, copy right from
//      900px, the same breakpoint and grid idea as Home's About block;
//      headshot above copy below 900px).
//   b. Studio — kept, at Sam's direction, overriding Kristen's "headshot
//      only" note. Amy's card is removed because her headshot now leads the
//      page. Sam and Kelsee unchanged; Reaghan Connelly's card is gated (see
//      REAGHAN below).
//   c. The "Let's Get Started" ContactBand.
// Hidden, not deleted: the ivory bay-window lead image (moving to /process,
// Task 7), the workroom stitching close-up, and all of the previous body copy
// (now src/content/pages/_hidden/about-before-copy-pass-v1.md). The two
// images are commented out in the markup below.
//
// Notes below this line describe the page as it was before that pass.
// Five required parts, in the brief's order:
// Amy's story, the origin section anchored to her grandmother's attic, the
// invention framing, the fabric lines, and the Studio row of three portraits.
//
// Copy sourced from the `pages` content collection (Phase 2 of the
// copy-bulk-swap work, BUILD-PLAN.md) — src/content/pages/about.md is now
// the one file to edit for this page's title, meta, lead, and all four body
// sections. The Studio row's three names/roles stay here, not in the
// collection: they're structured team data tightly coupled to three specific
// image imports, the same reasoning `projects.ts` already uses for
// photo-linked data.
//
// **Layout change from the copy-bulk-swap work: the origin (workroom) image
// moved.** It used to sit between "Where it started" and "Every one of them
// is invented," splitting the body prose into two `<RevealImage>`-separated
// halves. A single markdown document (matching every other page this phase
// converted) can't cleanly interleave an image mid-flow without a fragile
// parsing layer, so the image now sits after all four sections, immediately
// before Studio — workroom photo leading into the people who work in it,
// which reads fine as a sequence. Flagged here since it's a real, visible
// reordering, not just a refactor. Revisit if Sam or Amy would rather have
// it back in the middle badly enough to justify hand-splitting the page.
//
// **Known gap, deliberately not filled by invention.** 5.4.1 asks for "actual
// detail about what she made and for whom," and 5.4.2 wants the attic section
// to be specific. Those details exist only in Amy's head — ASK-AMY.md's first
// item is the recorded conversation that produces them. The copy is written
// at exactly the level of detail that is actually established (the attic,
// the trunks, taking things apart to see the construction) and stops there
// rather than inventing a first object, a first client, or a childhood
// scene. Expand this section from her own words, do not embellish it.
//
// Fabric lines: "the lines she represents" is the generic phrasing everywhere
// except here. Schumacher is the one house named anywhere on the public site,
// in the "Fabric" section's second paragraph below (about.md) — framed as
// where she has design access, not as a dealer/stockist/representative
// claim. /services/drapery, which used to name Schumacher too, was removed
// 2026-08-19 (post-Meeting-4 pass, Task 1). Stout and Pollack are not cleared
// and are named nowhere. **Standing rule, hardened 2026-08-19 (Task 4): Amy
// cannot represent herself as a dealer for any line — see CLAUDE.md, which
// names the blinds and shades vendor by name since that file is not public
// copy.** That vendor may not be named at all until she confirms otherwise
// in writing, and Schumacher may be named only as a source, never as a line
// the studio carries, represents, or deals.
//
// Images (IMAGE-MANIFEST.md standing rule): every slot carries a real photo.
// The origin section has no early photograph of Amy in existence on this
// machine, so the workroom shot stands in and is flagged in the manifest.

import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ContactBand from '../components/ContactBand.astro';
import RevealImage from '../components/RevealImage.astro';
import { getEntry, render } from 'astro:content';
import { photos } from '../data/photos';
import { coverSizes } from '../utils/coverSizes';
import originImage from '../assets/images/about/amy-hand-stitching-check-fabric-ottoman-cutting-table.jpg';
import samPortrait from '../assets/images/team/sam-clark.jpg';
import kelseePortrait from '../assets/images/team/kelsee-etmans.jpg';
import type { ImageMetadata } from 'astro';

const entry = await getEntry('pages', 'about');
const { Content } = await render(entry);
const { seoTitle, description, eyebrow, title, lede, lead, mission } = entry.data;

/* ---- STUDIO (updated 2026-10-12, POLISH-AND-AUDIT-V2 Task 3). ----
   Names, roles, and credential lines live here as plain data, one line each.
   Order: Sam, Kelsee, Reaghan. Amy has no card: her headshot leads the page
   (COPY-PASS-V1, Task 6), so the same photograph does not appear twice.
   Alt text is built from name + role, the pattern the cards always used.

   REAGHAN: her card renders only when BOTH are true at build time:
     1. src/assets/images/team/reaghan-connelly.jpg exists, and
     2. REAGHAN_CONNELLY_TITLE is not an empty string.
   `import.meta.glob` resolves to an empty object when the file is missing,
   so until the photo lands the row is Sam and Kelsee only: no empty slot, no
   placeholder, no broken image, and no build error. */
const REAGHAN_CONNELLY_TITLE = 'Social Media';

const STUDIO_PEOPLE = [
  { name: 'Sam Clark', role: 'Website and Digital Strategy', credential: 'Boston College' },
  { name: 'Kelsee Etmans', role: 'Photographer', credential: 'BFA, University of Cincinnati CCM' },
  {
    name: 'Reaghan Connelly',
    role: REAGHAN_CONNELLY_TITLE,
    credential: 'University of Cincinnati, Film and Media Studies',
  },
];

const reaghanPhoto = Object.values(
  import.meta.glob<{ default: ImageMetadata }>('../assets/images/team/reaghan-connelly.jpg', {
    eager: true,
  })
)[0]?.default;

// Photos and crop settings, keyed by name.
const STUDIO_PHOTOS: Record<string, { image?: ImageMetadata; blurDataURL?: string; lift?: boolean }> = {
  'Sam Clark': {
    image: samPortrait,
    // The only portrait that still needs a lifted crop — see the style block.
    lift: true,
    blurDataURL:
      'data:image/webp;base64,UklGRrgAAABXRUJQVlA4IKwAAADQBACdASoYAB4APwFqrU8rJiQiMAgBYCAJbACxHyGBlqVK7OZmAQYYc9pSMHaUAAD+zXxNENZ7PTGw6BXWhP3ISh6Sc+CivpasODVB5wfj+9w3pdDk5dlsVhWpamyDJvS1Q9FlRbFHkJQW1pdJx2Bu8g0HEJJpD8HKl5ZMBe93XZJLp0YhaMTxSHWnYfI3MGsZUFEZmi5Vd/+uEihbuAo6/EjYv2qJMgOKT4gA',
  },
  'Kelsee Etmans': {
    image: kelseePortrait,
    blurDataURL:
      'data:image/webp;base64,',
  },
  'Reaghan Connelly': { image: reaghanPhoto },
};

type StudioPerson = {
  image: ImageMetadata;
  alt: string;
  name: string;
  role: string;
  credential: string;
  lift?: boolean;
  blurDataURL?: string;
};
const studio: StudioPerson[] = STUDIO_PEOPLE.flatMap((person) => {
  const photo = STUDIO_PHOTOS[person.name];
  if (!photo?.image || !person.role.trim()) return [];
  return [
    {
      ...person,
      ...photo,
      image: photo.image,
      role: person.role.trim(),
      alt: `${person.name}, ${person.role.trim().toLowerCase()}`,
    },
  ];
});
---

<Base
  title={seoTitle}
  description={description}
  ogImage="/images/og/og-default.jpg"
  transparentNav={false}
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
    { name: 'About', href: '/about' },
  ]}
>
  <section class="section wrap about-intro">
    <div class="about-intro__grid">
      <figure class="about-intro__portrait">
        <RevealImage
          src={photos['amy-portrait'].image}
          alt={photos['amy-portrait'].alt}
          blurDataURL={photos['amy-portrait'].blurDataURL}
          aspectRatio="4/5"
          sizes={coverSizes(photos['amy-portrait'].image, 4 / 5, '(min-width: 900px) 24rem, 90vw')}
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
        />
      </figure>

      <div class="about-intro__copy">
        <p class="type-label text-page__eyebrow">{eyebrow}</p>
        <h1 class="type-display text-page__heading">{title}</h1>
        {lede && <p class="type-label about-intro__lede">{lede}</p>}
        {lead.map((paragraph) => <p class="text-page__lead">{paragraph}</p>)}
        <div class="prose about-intro__body">
          <Content />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* HIDDEN 2026-10-08 (COPY-PASS-V1, Task 6), not deleted. The ivory
      bay-window image moves to /process (Task 7); the stitching close-up is
      off the page. Restore by uncommenting.

  <RevealImage
    src={photos['ivory-house-bay-window'].image}
    alt={photos['ivory-house-bay-window'].alt}
    blurDataURL={photos['ivory-house-bay-window'].blurDataURL}
    aspectRatio="16/9"
    sizes="100vw"
  />

  <RevealImage
    src={originImage}
    alt="Amy's hands stitching a check-fabric ottoman on the workroom's gridded cutting table"
    blurDataURL="data:image/webp;base64,UklGRrQAAABXRUJQVlA4IKgAAAAQBQCdASoUABsAPtFWpk2oJCOiMBgIAQAaCUAWI+0YM6xTv/HqJLEODA5eoh4khh+AAP6A1FH/ibcZQuuEMg5Bb9qgUg+8MTeydH5d/BbmERZiGbJsiLRQ2+PUcm+DG+P8NtdDhDZFf1313HfX7lH3WkmsrO1kjqlzEbGk6qNAbfKC94avLNB3OZpndDKKEQGcZKeQXRVS3MhjogZaVWt6+6UBmAAAA="
    aspectRatio="16/9"
    sizes="100vw"
  />
  */}

  {/* Mission (POLISH-AND-AUDIT-V2, Task 3; Amy asked for one 2026-10-09).
      Copy in about.md. The heading is the same `.prose h2` as the About
      sections above it; the statement uses the testimonial-quote role at the
      existing subhead size, the site's largest non-heading text, so it reads
      as a statement rather than another paragraph. No new type styles. */}
  {mission && (
    <section class="section wrap about-mission" aria-labelledby="mission-heading">
      <div class="about-mission__grid">
        <div class="prose about-mission__copy">
          <h2 id="mission-heading">{mission.heading}</h2>
          <p class="type-quote text-page__subhead about-mission__statement">{mission.body}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  )}

  <section class="section wrap studio" aria-labelledby="studio-heading">
    <h2 id="studio-heading" class="type-display studio__heading">Studio</h2>
    <ul class="studio__list">
      {studio.map((person) => (
        <li class="studio__item">
          <figure class:list={['studio__figure', { 'studio__figure--lift': person.lift }]}>
            <RevealImage
              src={person.image}
              alt={person.alt}
              blurDataURL={person.blurDataURL}
              aspectRatio="1/1"
              sizes="(min-width: 768px) 30vw, 90vw"
            />
            <figcaption class="studio__caption">
              <p class="type-label studio__name">{person.name}</p>
              <p class="type-label studio__role">{person.role}</p>
              <p class="type-label studio__credential">{person.credential}</p>
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </section>

  <ContactBand />
</Base>

<style>
  /* ---- Headshot + copy (COPY-PASS-V1, Task 6). Portrait left, copy right
     from 900px, the same breakpoint and column logic as Home's About block
     (index.astro's `.differentiator__grid`), mirrored. DOM order is portrait
     then copy, which is also the mobile order Task 6 asks for. ---- */
  .about-intro__grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2.5rem;
  }

  .about-intro__portrait {
    max-width: 24rem;
    width: 100%;
  }

  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .about-intro__grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 24rem) minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 6rem);
      align-items: start;
    }
  }

  .about-intro__lede {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .about-intro__body {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  /* 5.4.5: "Three portraits in a row. Name in Label style, role beneath in
     --ink-muted. No biography paragraphs. Section heading is Studio, not Our
     Team." A plain three-up row, not a card grid — no border, no shadow, no
     radius, nothing the portraits sit inside (3.2). */
  .studio__heading {
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 1.2rem + 1.2vw, 2.25rem);
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .studio__list {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2.5rem;
  }

  /* Three tracks whether there are two cards or three (Reaghan's is gated,
     see the frontmatter), so a card is the same size either way and two
     cards simply leave the row short rather than growing to fill it. */
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .studio__list {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
      gap: 2rem;
    }
  }

  /* 1:1, not the 4:5 the rest of the site's images use. Still an asset
     constraint rather than a design preference, but a smaller one than it
     was: **Amy's real headshot landed 2026-07-27** (1941x1300, shot against
     white brick), replacing the ~400px circle-cropped avatar that was half
     the original reason for the square. Kelsee's is still that kind of
     avatar, and a 4:5 crop would slice her circle, so the row stays square
     until asset request 2 lands.

     The lifted object-position used to apply to all three figures. It only
     ever did real work on one: Sam's 888x1120 portrait, where a centred
     square crop shaves the top of his head. On the two near-square avatars
     there was almost no vertical overflow for it to act on, and on Amy's new
     landscape frame there is none at all — `cover` fills the square's height
     exactly, so the Y term is a no-op and a centred crop already lands her
     face well. Scoped to Sam alone rather than left blanket-applied.
     Revert the row to 4:5 the moment Kelsee's real headshot arrives. */
  .studio__figure--lift :global(.reveal-image__img) {
    object-position: 50% 15%;
  }

  .studio__caption {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  /* Credential line: the role line's own style (Label role, --ink-muted),
     so it never competes with the name. */
  .studio__credential {
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    /* Label's line-height is 1; a credential long enough to wrap
       (Reaghan's) needs room between its lines. */
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  /* Mission sits in the same column as the copy above it from 900px, so it
     reads as the end of Amy's section rather than a new page. Spacing only. */
  .about-mission {
    padding-top: 0;
  }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .about-mission__grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 24rem) minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 6rem);
    }
    .about-mission__copy {
      grid-column: 2;
    }
  }
  .about-mission__copy h2 {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .about-mission__statement {
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-bottom: 0;
    line-height: 1.35;
  }

  .studio__role {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }
  /* Image-first below 900px, and below 768px the section's 72px top padding
     only just equals the fixed nav's height, which left the photo pressed
     against the nav. A text-first page reads fine flush; a photo does not. */
  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .about-intro {
      padding-top: calc(var(--space-section) + 1.5rem);
    }
  }
</style>
